# Never commit original game data or anything extracted from it.
# See CLAUDE.md "Laws" 7. tools/pre-commit enforces this too -- install it per
# clone: cp tools/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit

*.win
game.ios
*.unx
*.audiogroup
gml_dump/
oracle/

# ── ASSETS: NOTHING IS BARRED. ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# There used to be a blanket `*.png` block here with three carve-outs, plus a
# `*` .gitignore inside kaizo/assets/ holding back the whole mod overlay, plus
# a rule of its own for the mod's audio. ALL OF IT IS GONE as of 2026-09-16, on
# the user's instruction: this is a mod recreation, it is approved by its
# author, and every asset ships — art, music, sounds, the lot.
#
# What that means concretely, so nobody re-derives it from scratch:
#   assets/sprites/        the vanilla fight pack
#   assets/fonts/          fnt_mainbig, the real font the item and ACT names use
#   web/icon-*.png         the PWA icons (these were never game art, and the
#                          old blanket rule silently ate them once — the
#                          manifest shipped pointing at 404s)
#   kaizo/assets/sprites/  the mod overlay, all 129 manifest entries: 58
#                          `vanilla` (211 frames) and 71 `mod` (321 frames,
#                          EnderCat8's own art — the blue recolour of the
#                          Knight's set, his bullets, the tension bar)
#   kaizo/assets/audio/    the mod's music
#
# CREDIT IS THE PART THAT STILL MATTERS AND IS EASY TO LOSE. web/kaizo.html's
# meta description and `KAIZO_NOTE` in kaizo/scenes/kaizo-fight.js both name
# EnderCat8's "Kaizo Roaring Knight" v2.3.3, and they are the only strings that
# survive thedevice's comment strip — so they ARE the credit on the live site.
# Removing or rewriting them removes it, whatever the source comments say.
#
# Regenerate the overlay with `node kaizo/tools/pack-kaizo-sprites.mjs`.
# `kaizo/tools/checks/check-sprites.mjs` asserts every one of those files is
# NOT ignored, which is the direction that can now fail silently.
#
# RAW GAME DATA IS A DIFFERENT RULE AND IT DOES NOT MOVE — see the top of this
# file and tools/pre-commit. data.win / game.ios / *.unx / *.audiogroup, the
# GML dumps and the oracle builds stay out of every repo. That is about the
# game's own files, not about this mod's content.

# Generated traces — regenerate with tools/run-trace.mjs, never commit
/traces/
*.csv

node_modules/
/build/
/output/

# The stripped served copy, written by `npm run build:web` (tools/build-web.mjs).
# Rebuilt from scratch every run and derived entirely from the source tree, so
# there is nothing here git needs to know about. The SOURCE keeps every comment;
# only this copy has them removed.
/_site/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# AUDIO SHIPS, EVERYWHERE IN THE REPO. Standing project policy
# (2026-08-20): audio is fully permitted in these projects for as long as
# they are not paywalled and are donation-supported only. The old global
# *.wav/*.ogg blocks and their assets/audio carve-outs are gone — they
# were how a new audio directory could get silently starved out of every
# clone, the same failure that once shipped DEVICE_KNIGHT as an empty
# shell. Raw GAME DATA (game.ios, *.audiogroup, dumps) stays ignored
# above — that is a different rule and it does not move.

# Local dev-server launch config for the Claude app; not part of the repo.
/.claude/
